From: silentsudin <25103587+silentsudin@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] VRR and frame pacing fixes from upstream gamescope 3.16.29/3.17.0

Applies on top of 0001-oxp3-hdr-pq.patch (Anatase gamescope 3.16.23.3).
Upstream ValveSoftware/gamescope commits, conflicts resolved against Anatase's
VRR keepalive and frame generation changes:
  - 3521d6bf steamcompmgr: allow uncapped frame rates with adaptive sync (Matthew Schwartz)
    (keeps Anatase's 10 Hz VRR keepalive: paint = (repaint && flip-ready) || keepalive)
  - c8fecc6c steamcompmgr: pace cursor repaints with content when adaptive sync is on (Matthew Schwartz)
  - c70f95e7 color: fix the native gamut blend on HDR10 output (Matthew Schwartz) (unit test dropped)
  - 62707e1e steamcompmgr: pace the frame limiter by display vblank (Matthew Schwartz)
    (frame generation keeps its own slot logic)
  - 261b9be1 steamcompmgr: keep the VRR frame limiter on its schedule (Matthew Schwartz)
  - 055902ca vblankmanager: leave deep idle ahead of a fixed refresh wakeup (Matthew Schwartz)
  - scripts: offer 30-47 Hz on the SDC AMS881KB01 OLED (silentsudin)
Not taken: 905a89bb (Anatase's frame generation patch already resolves the window
per commit), 8e0a5bee (Steam UI idle hold; deep conflicts with frame generation and
our HDR/VRR switching), 4d5b7f3c (changes the mangoapp message layout).
---
